{"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "chunk_id": "EXM-06:sec:PURPOSE", "content_sha256": "8d8c5d16f3e434405e616260f76ebecfa70580c6bce7dc9a2a47463f842dc02e", "heading": "Purpose", "kind": "section", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-017", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-ER-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "6162cc770e8391e4a76d68919b88fd9f23081ce9"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "", "research_family": "examiner_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": true, "mark_schemes": false, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "", "text": "# EXM-06 — Exam Technique Insights"}
{"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "chunk_id": "EXM-06:sec:PURPOSE", "content_sha256": "e82036242908be8c18d848d51f23b3d0e2d3a7dd234c1595622f88eaa3707d2c", "heading": "Purpose", "kind": "section", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-017", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-ER-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "6162cc770e8391e4a76d68919b88fd9f23081ce9"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "", "research_family": "examiner_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": true, "mark_schemes": false, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "", "text": "## Purpose\n\nThis artifact distils the exam-technique guidance embedded in the official 4CH1\nexaminer reports of the corpus of record (SRC-ER-4CH1): the behaviours the examiners\nexplicitly tell candidates to adopt — specify quantities exactly, write symbols\nlegibly, link explanation statements, read the method, read table keys correctly and\nrehearse practical technique. Every claim is carried on a bounded, page-located\nexcerpt from the run's evidence pack, with paper/session identity preserved.\nResearch artifact; canonical planes untouched."}
{"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "chunk_id": "EXM-06:sec:SCOPE", "content_sha256": "1250f98feaa6ee3ce41a85c87912275b9df01eb7feff64e1cc78d53226a7109f", "heading": "Scope", "kind": "section", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-017", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-ER-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "6162cc770e8391e4a76d68919b88fd9f23081ce9"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "", "research_family": "examiner_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": true, "mark_schemes": false, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "", "text": "## Scope\n\n**Covers:** six technique insights drawn from the 2023-2024 report excerpts of the\npack.\n\n**Grounding:** SRC-ER-4CH1 (the 2023-06 2C/2CR, 2023-11 1C/2C, 2024-06 1CR/2C/2CR and 2024-11 1C/2C excerpts of the pack, plus the appended 2019-06 2CR, 2022-06 1C and 2025-06 2C introductions).\n\n**Out of scope:** question-specific mechanics (EXM-05), penalty catalogue (EXM-04)."}
{"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "chunk_id": "EXM-06:sec:EXECUTIVE_SUMMARY", "content_sha256": "e0414066fa3f6eabe17172a56f4533aa50ee914ff0fd7367e68e1ac354b3b533", "heading": "Executive Summary", "kind": "section", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-017", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-ER-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "6162cc770e8391e4a76d68919b88fd9f23081ce9"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "", "research_family": "examiner_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": true, "mark_schemes": false, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "", "text": "## Executive Summary\n\nThe reports' technique advice is refreshingly concrete. Give values, not gestures: a\ncharge must be stated as -1, not as \"a minus sign with no value\". Write subscripts\nclearly, because ambiguous formulae lose marks regardless of the chemistry. In\nmulti-mark explanations, LINK the statements — the link is the mark. Read the method\nbefore answering: variable-control parts fail wholesale when the method is skipped.\nRead table keys correctly: relative atomic mass and atomic number sit in different\ncolumns. And treat practical questions as a rehearsed skill, since their performance\nis variable \"as always\". None of this is guesswork — every line is the board's own\nadvice to the next cohort."}
