{"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "chunk_id": "EXM-06:sec:LIMITATIONS_COVERAGE_GAPS", "content_sha256": "89a1d86da35cde94c9c20719e414e18eb95bd4865c6c2e607fa40737ca521b62", "heading": "Limitations / Coverage Gaps", "kind": "section", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-017", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-ER-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "6162cc770e8391e4a76d68919b88fd9f23081ce9"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "", "research_family": "examiner_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": true, "mark_schemes": false, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "", "text": "## Limitations / Coverage Gaps\n\nThe technique inventory covers the pack's 2023-2024 report excerpts and the appended 2019-06 2CR, 2022-06 1C and 2025-06 2C introductions; other held sessions sit in sibling packs. Sessions without public ERs remain source\ngaps of record. No canonical planes were written."}
{"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "chunk_id": "EXM-06:sec:RESEARCH_STATUS", "content_sha256": "ad287eb86659abc69f1af209a8c43b7673655c5b18447dad08476971139803d0", "heading": "Research Status", "kind": "section", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-017", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-ER-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "6162cc770e8391e4a76d68919b88fd9f23081ce9"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "", "research_family": "examiner_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": true, "mark_schemes": false, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "", "text": "## Research Status\n\nGENERATED under SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-005 (BL-008 pass 5) from the run's evidence\npack alone; validator of record tools/sib @ 357ace0a; claim QA r3 bound all citations\nto pack excerpts. Deepened under SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-017 (D3 tranche 1): +3 records (EXM-049..051) grounded in the pack of record, widened by disclosed diff-proved ER appends (2019-06 2CR / 2022-06 1C / 2025-06 2C p3); claim QA re-bound all citations. Research artifact — evidence-backed, not canonical educational truth."}
{"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "chunk_id": "EXM-06:rec:EXM-028", "content_sha256": "8a4f24d9bf2169803e039a23a4a4f229d36956c9a03f7b8e65906e9448dd0964", "heading": "EXM-028", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-017", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-ER-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "6162cc770e8391e4a76d68919b88fd9f23081ce9"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "EXM-028", "research_family": "examiner_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": true, "mark_schemes": false, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "EXM-028", "text": "### EXM-028 — Specify values exactly, not by gesture\n\n**Claim:** answers must give the exact value; an unquantified sign does not score.\n**Evidence:** \"The most common error was missing the charge – or giving the wrong\ncharge – for the electron. Some candidates simply gave a minus sign with no value:\nit did need to be – 1 in order to be equal (but opposite) the charge on a proton.\"\n(SRC-ER-4CH1, 2023-06/4CH1-2CR/er.pdf p4).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "chunk_id": "EXM-06:rec:EXM-029", "content_sha256": "5d4cbb6e0931ccd8c480c6a63bc2efd821204c9dec58c152f03112d6399ba738", "heading": "EXM-029", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-017", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-ER-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "6162cc770e8391e4a76d68919b88fd9f23081ce9"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "EXM-029", "research_family": "examiner_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": true, "mark_schemes": false, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "EXM-029", "text": "### EXM-029 — Write chemical symbols legibly\n\n**Claim:** subscripts and formulae must be unambiguous.\n**Evidence:** \"Candidates need to take care to write their subscript numbers clearly\nwh...\" — the 2023-11 1C formula-work advice (SRC-ER-4CH1, 2023-11/4CH1-1C/er.pdf p4).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "chunk_id": "EXM-06:rec:EXM-030", "content_sha256": "502808211eefdee1094b8247c6221877e50c14b3f87551abf688d8b091267083", "heading": "EXM-030", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-017", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-ER-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "6162cc770e8391e4a76d68919b88fd9f23081ce9"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "EXM-030", "research_family": "examiner_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": true, "mark_schemes": false, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "EXM-030", "text": "### EXM-030 — Link the statements in extended explanations\n\n**Claim:** multi-mark explanations pay for the link, not the statements alone.\n**Evidence:** \"Many of the candidates struggled with these questions and only the\nvery best scored full marks. They needed to link the statements to gain all the\nmarks\" (SRC-ER-4CH1, 2024-06/4CH1-1CR/er.pdf p3).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "chunk_id": "EXM-06:rec:EXM-031", "content_sha256": "c78ca817cf63033b910cb83d49c87505c20f5e80f67b613e707db86ffa1171ae", "heading": "EXM-031", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-017", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-ER-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "6162cc770e8391e4a76d68919b88fd9f23081ce9"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "EXM-031", "research_family": "examiner_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": true, "mark_schemes": false, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "EXM-031", "text": "### EXM-031 — Read the method and its variable-control design\n\n**Claim:** method-led parts fail wholesale when the printed method is skipped.\n**Evidence:** \"It appears that the candidates either did not read the method or did\nnot understand the idea of keeping the variables constant. As the acid was added\ninitially there could not be a change in the volume, concentration or initial\ntemperature.\" (SRC-ER-4CH1, 2023-11/4CH1-2C/er.pdf p4).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "chunk_id": "EXM-06:rec:EXM-032", "content_sha256": "bcd5bef2401869abc33d31f07fe21800012da53798fa82efba1afbd3e9142319", "heading": "EXM-032", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-017", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-ER-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "6162cc770e8391e4a76d68919b88fd9f23081ce9"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "EXM-032", "research_family": "examiner_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": true, "mark_schemes": false, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "EXM-032", "text": "### EXM-032 — Read the table keys correctly\n\n**Claim:** data-table literacy (RAM vs atomic number columns) is an examined\ntechnique.\n**Evidence:** \"A small minority confused relative atomic mass with atomic number and\nwrote nitrogen, even though the key on the Periodic Table showed where the atomic\nnumber was.\" (SRC-ER-4CH1, 2023-06/4CH1-2C/er.pdf p4).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "chunk_id": "EXM-06:rec:EXM-033", "content_sha256": "96ef73ec5847ddcf24bf56bb9d168d611680453f570b19834848d41fddf24c30", "heading": "EXM-033", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-017", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-ER-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "6162cc770e8391e4a76d68919b88fd9f23081ce9"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "EXM-033", "research_family": "examiner_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": true, "mark_schemes": false, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "EXM-033", "text": "### EXM-033 — Practical questions reward rehearsed technique\n\n**Claim:** the reports flag practical-situation questions as a persistent variability\n— and definition-level precision as a weak spot.\n**Evidence:** \"Questions on practical situations, as always, produced a variable\"\nfollowed by the alloy observation \"Candidates answered the question about an alloy's\nproperties, but were less sure about a definition for an alloy.\" (SRC-ER-4CH1, 2023-06/4CH1-2CR/er.pdf p3).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "chunk_id": "EXM-06:rec:EXM-049", "content_sha256": "83183ef2cbc7cb2454d90dd6b7c20cf78a3f2fe57c466d9d343f5e0bd2172cdd", "heading": "EXM-049", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-017", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-ER-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "6162cc770e8391e4a76d68919b88fd9f23081ce9"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "EXM-049", "research_family": "examiner_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": true, "mark_schemes": false, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "EXM-049", "text": "### EXM-049 — Draft-then-tick: the extended-response discipline\n\n**Claim:** the stated extended-response technique is draft-then-tick — draft ideas first and tick off question parts as they appear in the answer. The technique costs no chemistry time and addresses the session's named failure mode — extended answers that drift off the printed demands. It is the examiner's own proposed study skill, stated in the report's voice.\n**Evidence:** \"should be encouraged to draft their ideas first or tick parts of the question off when they appear in the answer\" (SRC-ER-4CH1, 2022-06/4CH1-1C/er.pdf p3).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "chunk_id": "EXM-06:rec:EXM-050", "content_sha256": "bd7dfa13a1aff4b691e62f3df2154267c1171ec4f5c692cddadcef3c4a479a75", "heading": "EXM-050", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-017", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-ER-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "6162cc770e8391e4a76d68919b88fd9f23081ce9"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "EXM-050", "research_family": "examiner_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": true, "mark_schemes": false, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "EXM-050", "text": "### EXM-050 — Answer the demand: description is not explanation\n\n**Claim:** demand discipline is a stated examiner expectation — a description part does not want an explanation. The same 2CR session had just watched candidates volunteer intermolecular-force explanations into a description part, so the reminder is the vagueness warning spent from the other side: answer exactly the demand printed, no more and no less.\n**Evidence:** \"Candidates need to realise that if the question asks for a description an explanation is not required.\" (SRC-ER-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-2CR/er.pdf p3).\n; \"Quite a few candidates felt the need to explain the differences in terms of intermolecular forces.\" (SRC-ER-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-2CR/er.pdf p3).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "chunk_id": "EXM-06:rec:EXM-051", "content_sha256": "dc40454e20722883ae530d767ebac43fbee60285df8d1af0863222efff6907f6", "heading": "EXM-051", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "EXM-06", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-017", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-ER-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "6162cc770e8391e4a76d68919b88fd9f23081ce9"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "EXM-051", "research_family": "examiner_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": true, "mark_schemes": false, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "EXM-051", "text": "### EXM-051 — The equilibrium-arrow marking law\n\n**Claim:** equilibrium-arrow notation carries an explicit marking law as of 2025-06 2C Q02(e): directional arrows only. The ruling is dated and paper-specific on its face, but its direction is general: equilibrium notation is examined for direction sense, and legacy habits — double arrows, bare lines — now cost the mark. The same introduction flags Q02(e)'s question as unusual and discriminating.\n**Evidence:** \"Q02(e) is no longer allowed for double arrows or just straight lines. It has to be arrows shown in the right directions.\" (SRC-ER-4CH1, 2025-06/4CH1-2C/er.pdf p3).\n; \"Question 2 was unusual and discriminated well.\" (SRC-ER-4CH1, 2025-06/4CH1-2C/er.pdf p3).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
